#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Un cours IBM gratuit sur l'information et le calcul quantiques"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: sidebar_label
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inner products and projections"
msgstr "Produits scalaires et projections"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* cspell:ignore Biggr, operatorname */}\n"
"To better prepare ourselves to explore the capabilities and limitations of quantum circuits, we now introduce some additional mathematical concepts — namely the *inner product* between vectors (and its connection to the Euclidean norm), the notions of *orthogonality* and *orthonormality* for sets of vectors, and *projection* matrices, which will allow us to introduce a handy generalization of standard basis measurements.\n"
msgstr ""
"{/* cspell:ignore Biggr, operatorname */}\n"
"Pour mieux nous préparer à explorer les capacités et les limites des circuits quantiques, nous introduisons maintenant quelques concepts mathématiques supplémentaires — à savoir le *produit scalaire* entre vecteurs (et son lien avec la norme euclidienne), les notions d'*orthogonalité* et d'*orthonormalité* pour des ensembles de vecteurs, ainsi que les matrices de *projection*, qui nous permettront d'introduire une généralisation pratique des mesures dans la base standard.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Inner products {#inner-products}"
msgstr "Produits scalaires {#inner-products}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recall that when we use the Dirac notation to refer to an arbitrary column "
"vector as a ket, such as\n"
msgstr ""
"Rappelle-toi que lorsqu'on utilise la notation de Dirac pour désigner un "
"vecteur colonne arbitraire par un ket, tel que\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_1\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_1\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"the corresponding bra vector is the *conjugate transpose* of this vector:\n"
msgstr ""
"le vecteur bra correspondant est le *conjugué transposé* de ce vecteur :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert = \\bigl(\\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert = \\bigl(\\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"=\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\overline{\\alpha_2} & \\cdots & \\overline{\\alpha_n}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\overline{\\alpha_2} & \\cdots & \\overline{\\alpha_n}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alternatively, if we have some classical state set $\\Sigma$ in mind, and we express a column vector as a ket,\n"
"such as\n"
msgstr ""
"Alternativement, si on a un ensemble d'états classiques $\\Sigma$ en tête, et qu'on exprime un vecteur colonne sous forme de ket,\n"
"tel que\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "then the corresponding row (or bra) vector is the conjugate transpose\n"
msgstr ""
"alors le vecteur ligne (ou bra) correspondant est le conjugué transposé\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\langle a \\vert.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\langle a \\vert.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We also have that the product of a bra vector and a ket vector, viewed as matrices either having a single row or a single column, results in a scalar.\n"
"Specifically, if we have two column vectors\n"
msgstr ""
"On a également que le produit d'un vecteur bra et d'un vecteur ket, considérés comme des matrices ayant respectivement une seule ligne ou une seule colonne, donne un scalaire.\n"
"Plus précisément, si on a deux vecteurs colonnes\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_1\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\phi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\beta_1\\\\\n"
"\\beta_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\beta_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_1\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad\\text{et}\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\phi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\beta_1\\\\\n"
"\\beta_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\beta_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "so that the row vector $\\langle \\psi \\vert$ is as in equation $(1),$ then\n"
msgstr ""
"de sorte que le vecteur ligne $\\langle \\psi \\vert$ est comme dans "
"l'équation $(1),$ alors\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\overline{\\alpha_2} & \\cdots & \\overline{\\alpha_n}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\beta_1\\\\\n"
"\\beta_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\beta_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\beta_1 + \\cdots + \\overline{\\alpha_n}\\beta_n.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\overline{\\alpha_2} & \\cdots & \\overline{\\alpha_n}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\beta_1\\\\\n"
"\\beta_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\beta_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\beta_1 + \\cdots + \\overline{\\alpha_n}\\beta_n.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Alternatively, if we have two column vectors that we have written as\n"
msgstr ""
"Alternativement, si on a deux vecteurs colonnes qu'on a écrits sous la "
"forme\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"\\quad\\text{et}\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "so that $\\langle \\psi \\vert$ is the row vector $(2),$ we find that\n"
msgstr ""
"de sorte que $\\langle \\psi \\vert$ est le vecteur ligne $(2),$ on trouve "
"que\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle & = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\vert \\phi \\rangle\\\\\n"
"  & =\n"
"  \\Biggl(\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\langle a \\vert\\Biggr)\n"
"  \\Biggl(\\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b\\rangle\\Biggr)\\\\\n"
"  & =\n"
"  \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma}\\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_b \\langle a \\vert b \\rangle\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_a,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle & = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\vert \\phi \\rangle\\\\\n"
"  & =\n"
"  \\Biggl(\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\langle a \\vert\\Biggr)\n"
"  \\Biggl(\\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b\\rangle\\Biggr)\\\\\n"
"  & =\n"
"  \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma}\\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_b \\langle a \\vert b \\rangle\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_a,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where the last equality follows from the observation that $\\langle a \\vert"
" a \\rangle = 1$ and $\\langle a \\vert b \\rangle = 0$ for classical states"
" $a$ and $b$ satisfying $a\\neq b.$\n"
msgstr ""
"où la dernière égalité découle de l'observation que $\\langle a \\vert a "
"\\rangle = 1$ et $\\langle a \\vert b \\rangle = 0$ pour des états "
"classiques $a$ et $b$ satisfaisant $a\\neq b.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The value $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle$ is called the *inner product* between the vectors $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ and $\\vert \\phi \\rangle.$\n"
"Inner products are critically important in quantum information and computation;\n"
"we would not get far in understanding quantum information at a mathematical level without them.\n"
msgstr ""
"La valeur $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle$ est appelée le *produit scalaire* entre les vecteurs $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ et $\\vert \\phi \\rangle.$\n"
"Les produits scalaires sont d'une importance capitale en information et en calcul quantiques ;\n"
"on ne pourrait pas aller bien loin dans la compréhension mathématique de l'information quantique sans eux.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let us now collect together some basic facts about inner products of "
"vectors.\n"
msgstr ""
"Rassemblons maintenant quelques propriétés fondamentales des produits "
"scalaires de vecteurs.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Relationship to the Euclidean norm.** The inner product of any vector\n"
msgstr "**Lien avec la norme euclidienne.** Le produit scalaire d'un vecteur\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "   with itself is\n"
msgstr "   avec lui-même vaut\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle\n"
"   = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\alpha_a\n"
"   = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert\\alpha_a\\vert^2\n"
"   = \\bigl\\| \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle\n"
"   = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\alpha_a\n"
"   = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert\\alpha_a\\vert^2\n"
"   = \\bigl\\| \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Thus, the Euclidean norm of a vector may alternatively be expressed as\n"
msgstr ""
"   Ainsi, la norme euclidienne d'un vecteur peut aussi s'exprimer comme\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl\\| \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\| = \\sqrt{ \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle }.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl\\| \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\| = \\sqrt{ \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle }.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Notice that the Euclidean norm of a vector must always be a nonnegative real number.\n"
"   Moreover, the only way the Euclidean norm of a vector can be equal to zero is if every one of the entries is equal to zero, which is to say that the vector is the zero vector.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Note que la norme euclidienne d'un vecteur est toujours un nombre réel non négatif.\n"
"   De plus, la seule façon pour que la norme euclidienne d'un vecteur soit nulle est que toutes ses entrées soient nulles, c'est-à-dire que le vecteur soit le vecteur nul.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   We can summarize these observations like this: for every vector $\\vert "
"\\psi \\rangle$ we have\n"
msgstr ""
"   On peut résumer ces observations ainsi : pour tout vecteur $\\vert \\psi "
"\\rangle$ on a\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\geq 0,\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\geq 0,\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   with $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle = 0$ if and only if $\\vert \\psi \\rangle = 0.$\n"
"   This property of the inner product is sometimes referred to as _positive definiteness_.\n"
msgstr ""
"   avec $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle = 0$ si et seulement si $\\vert \\psi \\rangle = 0.$\n"
"   Cette propriété du produit scalaire est parfois appelée _définie positive_.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Conjugate symmetry.** For any two vectors\n"
msgstr "**Symétrie conjuguée.** Pour deux vecteurs quelconques\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"   \\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"   \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b \\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"   \\quad\\text{et}\\quad\n"
"   \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b \\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "   we have\n"
msgstr "   on a\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_a\n"
"   \\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"   \\langle \\phi \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\beta_a} \\alpha_a,\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_a\n"
"   \\quad\\text{et}\\quad\n"
"   \\langle \\phi \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\beta_a} \\alpha_a,\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "   and therefore\n"
msgstr "   et donc\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\overline{\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle} = \\langle \\phi \\vert \\psi \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\overline{\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle} = \\langle \\phi \\vert \\psi \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Linearity in the second argument (and conjugate linearity in the first).**\n"
"Let us suppose that $\\vert \\psi \\rangle,$ $\\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle,$ and $\\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle$ are vectors and $\\alpha_1$ and $\\alpha_2$ are complex numbers. If we define a new vector\n"
msgstr ""
"**Linéarité par rapport au second argument (et linéarité conjuguée par rapport au premier).**\n"
"Supposons que $\\vert \\psi \\rangle,$ $\\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle,$ et $\\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle$ sont des vecteurs et que $\\alpha_1$ et $\\alpha_2$ sont des nombres complexes. Si on définit un nouveau vecteur\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\phi\\rangle = \\alpha_1 \\vert \\phi_1\\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\vert \\phi_2\\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\phi\\rangle = \\alpha_1 \\vert \\phi_1\\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\vert \\phi_2\\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "   then\n"
msgstr "   alors\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigl( \\alpha_1\\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle + \\alpha_2\\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"   = \\alpha_1 \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigl( \\alpha_1\\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle + \\alpha_2\\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"   = \\alpha_1 \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   That is to say, the inner product is _linear_ in the second argument.\n"
"   This can be verified either through the formulas above or simply by noting that matrix multiplication is linear in each argument (and specifically in the second argument).\n"
msgstr ""
"   Autrement dit, le produit scalaire est _linéaire_ par rapport au second argument.\n"
"   Cela peut se vérifier soit par les formules ci-dessus, soit simplement en remarquant que la multiplication matricielle est linéaire par rapport à chaque argument (et en particulier par rapport au second argument).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Combining this fact with conjugate symmetry reveals that the inner "
"product is _conjugate linear_ in the first argument. That is, if $\\vert "
"\\psi_1 \\rangle,$ $\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle,$ and $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ "
"are vectors and $\\alpha_1$ and $\\alpha_2$ are complex numbers, and we "
"define\n"
msgstr ""
"   En combinant ce fait avec la symétrie conjuguée, on conclut que le "
"produit scalaire est _conjugué linéaire_ par rapport au premier argument. "
"C'est-à-dire que si $\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle,$ $\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle,$ et"
" $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ sont des vecteurs et $\\alpha_1$ et $\\alpha_2$ "
"sont des nombres complexes, et qu'on définit\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\alpha_1 \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\alpha_1 \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   =\n"
"   \\bigl( \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\langle \\psi_1 \\vert + \\overline{\\alpha_2} \\langle \\psi_2 \\vert \\bigr)\n"
"   \\vert\\phi\\rangle\n"
"   = \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\langle \\psi_1 \\vert \\phi \\rangle + \\overline{\\alpha_2} \\langle \\psi_2 \\vert \\phi \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   =\n"
"   \\bigl( \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\langle \\psi_1 \\vert + \\overline{\\alpha_2} \\langle \\psi_2 \\vert \\bigr)\n"
"   \\vert\\phi\\rangle\n"
"   = \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\langle \\psi_1 \\vert \\phi \\rangle + \\overline{\\alpha_2} \\langle \\psi_2 \\vert \\phi \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The Cauchy–Schwarz inequality.**\n"
"For every choice of vectors $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ and $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ having the same number of entries, we have\n"
msgstr ""
"**L'inégalité de Cauchy–Schwarz.**\n"
"Pour tout choix de vecteurs $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ et $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ ayant le même nombre d'entrées, on a\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl\\vert \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\\bigr| \\leq \\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\| \\bigl\\| \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   \\bigr\\|.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl\\vert \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\\bigr| \\leq \\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\| \\bigl\\| \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   \\bigr\\|.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   This is an incredibly handy inequality that gets used quite extensively "
"in quantum information (and in many other topics of study).\n"
msgstr ""
"   C'est une inégalité incroyablement pratique, très largement utilisée en "
"information quantique (et dans de nombreux autres domaines d'étude).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Orthogonal and orthonormal sets {#orthogonal-and-orthonormal-sets}"
msgstr ""
"Ensembles orthogonaux et orthonormaux {#orthogonal-and-orthonormal-sets}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Two vectors $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ and $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ are said to "
"be *orthogonal* if their inner product is zero:\n"
msgstr ""
"On dit que deux vecteurs $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ et $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ "
"sont *orthogonaux* si leur produit scalaire est nul :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = 0.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = 0.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Geometrically, we can think about orthogonal vectors as vectors at right "
"angles to each other.\n"
msgstr ""
"Géométriquement, on peut voir les vecteurs orthogonaux comme des vecteurs "
"perpendiculaires l'un à l'autre.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A set of vectors $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ is called an *orthogonal set* if every vector in the set is orthogonal to every other vector in the set.\n"
"That is, this set is orthogonal if\n"
msgstr ""
"Un ensemble de vecteurs $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ est appelé un *ensemble orthogonal* si chaque vecteur de l'ensemble est orthogonal à tous les autres vecteurs de l'ensemble.\n"
"C'est-à-dire que cet ensemble est orthogonal si\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_j \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle = 0\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_j \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle = 0\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for all choices of $j,k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,m\\}$ for which $j\\neq k.$\n"
msgstr "pour tous les choix de $j,k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,m\\}$ tels que $j\\neq k.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A set of vectors $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ is called an *orthonormal* set if it is an orthogonal set and, in addition, every vector in the set is a unit vector.\n"
"Alternatively, this set is an orthonormal set if we have\n"
msgstr ""
"Un ensemble de vecteurs $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ est appelé un ensemble *orthonormal* s'il est orthogonal et si, de plus, chaque vecteur de l'ensemble est un vecteur unitaire.\n"
"Alternativement, cet ensemble est orthonormal si\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_j \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & j = k\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & j\\neq k\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\tag{3}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_j \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & j = k\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & j\\neq k\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\tag{3}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for all choices of $j,k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,m\\}.$\n"
msgstr "pour tous les choix de $j,k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,m\\}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, a set $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ is an *orthonormal basis* if, in addition to being an orthonormal set, it forms a basis.\n"
"This is equivalent to $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ being an orthonormal set and $m$ being equal to the dimension of the space from which $\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle$ are drawn.\n"
msgstr ""
"Enfin, un ensemble $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ est une *base orthonormale* si, en plus d'être un ensemble orthonormal, il forme une base.\n"
"Cela est équivalent à dire que $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ est un ensemble orthonormal et que $m$ est égal à la dimension de l'espace d'où sont tirés $\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, for any classical state set $\\Sigma,$ the set of all standard "
"basis vectors\n"
msgstr ""
"Par exemple, pour tout ensemble d'états classiques $\\Sigma,$ l'ensemble de "
"tous les vecteurs de la base standard\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\big\\{ \\vert a \\rangle \\,:\\, a\\in\\Sigma\\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\big\\{ \\vert a \\rangle \\,:\\, a\\in\\Sigma\\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"is an orthonormal basis.\n"
"The set $\\{\\vert+\\rangle,\\vert-\\rangle\\}$ is an orthonormal basis for the $2$-dimensional space corresponding to a single qubit, and the Bell basis $\\{\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle, \\vert\\phi^-\\rangle, \\vert\\psi^+\\rangle, \\vert\\psi^-\\rangle\\}$ is an orthonormal basis for the $4$-dimensional space corresponding to two qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"est une base orthonormale.\n"
"L'ensemble $\\{\\vert+\\rangle,\\vert-\\rangle\\}$ est une base orthonormale pour l'espace de dimension $2$ correspondant à un seul qubit, et la base de Bell $\\{\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle, \\vert\\phi^-\\rangle, \\vert\\psi^+\\rangle, \\vert\\psi^-\\rangle\\}$ est une base orthonormale pour l'espace de dimension $4$ correspondant à deux qubits.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Extending orthonormal sets to orthonormal bases {#extending-orthonormal-"
"sets-to-orthonormal-bases}"
msgstr ""
"Compléter des ensembles orthonormaux en bases orthonormales {#extending-"
"orthonormal-sets-to-orthonormal-bases}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose that $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle$ are vectors that live in an $n$-dimensional space, and assume moreover that $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ is an orthonormal set.\n"
"Orthonormal sets are always linearly independent sets, so these vectors necessarily span a subspace of dimension $m.$\n"
"From this we conclude that $m\\leq n$ because the dimension of the subspace spanned by these vectors cannot be larger than the dimension of the entire space from which they're drawn.\n"
msgstr ""
"Supposons que $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle$ sont des vecteurs vivant dans un espace de dimension $n$, et qu'en plus $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ est un ensemble orthonormal.\n"
"Les ensembles orthonormaux sont toujours des ensembles linéairement indépendants, donc ces vecteurs engendrent nécessairement un sous-espace de dimension $m.$\n"
"On en conclut que $m\\leq n$, car la dimension du sous-espace engendré par ces vecteurs ne peut pas être supérieure à la dimension de l'espace entier dont ils sont tirés.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If it is the case that $m<n,$ then it is always possible to choose an additional $n-m$ vectors\n"
"$\\vert \\psi_{m+1}\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle$ so that\n"
"$\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\}$ forms an orthonormal basis.\n"
"A procedure known as the *Gram–Schmidt orthogonalization process* can be used to construct these vectors.\n"
msgstr ""
"Si $m<n,$ il est toujours possible de choisir $n-m$ vecteurs supplémentaires\n"
"$\\vert \\psi_{m+1}\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle$ de sorte que\n"
"$\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\}$ forme une base orthonormale.\n"
"Une procédure connue sous le nom de *procédé d'orthogonalisation de Gram–Schmidt* peut être utilisée pour construire ces vecteurs.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Orthonormal sets and unitary matrices {#orthonormal-sets-and-unitary-"
"matrices}"
msgstr ""
"Ensembles orthonormaux et matrices unitaires {#orthonormal-sets-and-unitary-"
"matrices}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Orthonormal sets of vectors are closely connected with unitary matrices.\n"
"One way to express this connection is to say that the following three statements are logically equivalent (meaning that they are all true or all false) for any choice of a square matrix $U$:\n"
msgstr ""
"Les ensembles orthonormaux de vecteurs sont étroitement liés aux matrices unitaires.\n"
"Une façon d'exprimer ce lien est de dire que les trois affirmations suivantes sont logiquement équivalentes (c'est-à-dire qu'elles sont toutes vraies ou toutes fausses) pour tout choix d'une matrice carrée $U$ :\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The matrix $U$ is unitary (that is, $U^{\\dagger} U = \\mathbb{I} = U "
"U^{\\dagger}$).\n"
msgstr ""
"La matrice $U$ est unitaire (c'est-à-dire $U^{\\dagger} U = \\mathbb{I} = U "
"U^{\\dagger}$).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The rows of $U$ form an orthonormal set.\n"
msgstr "Les lignes de $U$ forment un ensemble orthonormal.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The columns of $U$ form an orthonormal set.\n"
msgstr "Les colonnes de $U$ forment un ensemble orthonormal.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This equivalence is actually pretty straightforward when we think about how matrix multiplication and the conjugate transpose work.\n"
"Suppose, for instance, that we have a $3\\times 3$ matrix like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"Cette équivalence est en réalité assez directe lorsqu'on réfléchit au fonctionnement de la multiplication matricielle et du conjugué transposé.\n"
"Supposons par exemple qu'on ait une matrice $3\\times 3$ comme celle-ci :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1} & \\alpha_{1,2} & \\alpha_{1,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1} & \\alpha_{2,2} & \\alpha_{2,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1} & \\alpha_{3,2} & \\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1} & \\alpha_{1,2} & \\alpha_{1,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1} & \\alpha_{2,2} & \\alpha_{2,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1} & \\alpha_{3,2} & \\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The conjugate transpose of $U$ looks like this:\n"
msgstr "Le conjugué transposé de $U$ ressemble à ceci :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U^{\\dagger} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U^{\\dagger} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Multiplying the two matrices, with the conjugate transpose on the left-hand "
"side, gives us this matrix:\n"
msgstr ""
"Le produit des deux matrices, avec le conjugué transposé à gauche, nous "
"donne la matrice suivante :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"&\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1} & \\alpha_{1,2} & \\alpha_{1,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1} & \\alpha_{2,2} & \\alpha_{2,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1} & \\alpha_{3,2} & \\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\quad &=\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,3} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,3} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"&\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1} & \\alpha_{1,2} & \\alpha_{1,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1} & \\alpha_{2,2} & \\alpha_{2,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1} & \\alpha_{3,2} & \\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\quad &=\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,3} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,3} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "If we form three vectors from the columns of $U,$\n"
msgstr "Si on forme trois vecteurs à partir des colonnes de $U,$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\psi_2\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,2}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,2}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\psi_3\\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,3}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,3}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\psi_2\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,2}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,2}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\psi_3\\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,3}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,3}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "then we can alternatively express the product above as follows:\n"
msgstr "on peut alors exprimer le produit ci-dessus autrement :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U^{\\dagger} U =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U^{\\dagger} U =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Referring to the equation $(3),$ we now see that the condition that this "
"matrix is equal to the identity matrix is equivalent to the orthonormality "
"of the set "
"$\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_2\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_3\\rangle\\}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"En se référant à l'équation $(3),$ on voit maintenant que la condition que "
"cette matrice soit égale à la matrice identité est équivalente à "
"l'orthonormalité de l'ensemble "
"$\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_2\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_3\\rangle\\}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This argument generalizes to unitary matrices of any size.\n"
"The fact that the rows of a matrix form an orthonormal basis if and only if the matrix is unitary then follows from the fact that a matrix is unitary if and only if its transpose is unitary.\n"
msgstr ""
"Cet argument se généralise aux matrices unitaires de toute taille.\n"
"Le fait que les lignes d'une matrice forment une base orthonormale si et seulement si la matrice est unitaire découle alors du fait qu'une matrice est unitaire si et seulement si sa transposée est unitaire.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given the equivalence described above, together with the fact that every orthonormal set can be extended to form an orthonormal basis, we conclude the following useful fact:\n"
"Given any orthonormal set of vectors $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ drawn from an $n$-dimensional space, there exists a unitary matrix $U$ whose first $m$ columns are the vectors $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle.$\n"
"Pictorially, we can always find a unitary matrix having this form:\n"
msgstr ""
"Compte tenu de l'équivalence décrite ci-dessus, et du fait que tout ensemble orthonormal peut être complété en une base orthonormale, on conclut le fait utile suivant :\n"
"Étant donné un ensemble orthonormal quelconque de vecteurs $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ tirés d'un espace de dimension $n$, il existe une matrice unitaire $U$ dont les $m$ premières colonnes sont les vecteurs $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle.$\n"
"Schématiquement, on peut toujours trouver une matrice unitaire de la forme suivante :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U =\n"
"\\left(\n"
"  \\begin{array}{ccccccc}\n"
"    \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt}\\\\\n"
"    \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle & \\vert\\psi_2\\rangle & \\cdots & \\vert\\psi_m\\rangle & \\vert\\psi_{m+1}\\rangle &\n"
"    \\cdots & \\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"    \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt}\n"
"  \\end{array}\n"
"\\right).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U =\n"
"\\left(\n"
"  \\begin{array}{ccccccc}\n"
"    \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt}\\\\\n"
"    \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle & \\vert\\psi_2\\rangle & \\cdots & \\vert\\psi_m\\rangle & \\vert\\psi_{m+1}\\rangle &\n"
"    \\cdots & \\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"    \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt}\n"
"  \\end{array}\n"
"\\right).\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, the last $n-m$ columns are filled in with any choice of vectors $\\vert\\psi_{m+1}\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle$ that make\n"
"$\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\}$ an orthonormal basis.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ici, les $n-m$ dernières colonnes sont complétées par un choix quelconque de vecteurs $\\vert\\psi_{m+1}\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle$ qui font de\n"
"$\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\}$ une base orthonormale.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Projections and projective measurements {#projections-and-projective-"
"measurements}"
msgstr ""
"Projections et mesures projectives {#projections-and-projective-"
"measurements}"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Projection matrices {#projection-matrices}"
msgstr "Matrices de projection {#projection-matrices}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A square matrix $\\Pi$ is called a *projection* if it satisfies two "
"properties:\n"
msgstr ""
"Une matrice carrée $\\Pi$ est appelée *projection* si elle satisfait deux "
"propriétés :\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$\\Pi = \\Pi^{\\dagger}.$\n"
msgstr "$\\Pi = \\Pi^{\\dagger}.$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$\\Pi^2 = \\Pi.$\n"
msgstr "$\\Pi^2 = \\Pi.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Matrices that satisfy the first condition — that they are equal to their own"
" conjugate transpose — are called *Hermitian matrices*, and matrices that "
"satisfy the second condition — that squaring them leaves them unchanged — "
"are called *idempotent* matrices.\n"
msgstr ""
"Les matrices qui satisfont la première condition — être égales à leur propre"
" conjugué transposé — sont appelées *matrices hermitiennes*, et les matrices"
" qui satisfont la seconde condition — dont le carré ne les modifie pas — "
"sont appelées matrices *idempotentes*.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As a word of caution, the word *projection* is sometimes used to refer to any matrix that satisfies just the second condition but not necessarily the first, and when this is done the term *orthogonal projection* is typically used to refer to matrices satisfying both properties.\n"
"In the context of quantum information and computation, however, the terms *projection* and *projection matrix* more typically refer to matrices satisfying both conditions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Par précaution, le mot *projection* est parfois utilisé pour désigner toute matrice qui ne satisfait que la seconde condition mais pas nécessairement la première, et dans ce cas le terme *projection orthogonale* désigne typiquement les matrices satisfaisant les deux propriétés.\n"
"Dans le contexte de l'information et du calcul quantiques, cependant, les termes *projection* et *matrice de projection* désignent plus généralement des matrices satisfaisant les deux conditions.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "An example of a projection is the matrix\n"
msgstr "Un exemple de projection est la matrice\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi = \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert\n"
"\\tag{4}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi = \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert\n"
"\\tag{4}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for any unit vector $\\vert \\psi\\rangle.$\n"
"We can see that this matrix is Hermitian as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"pour tout vecteur unitaire $\\vert \\psi\\rangle.$\n"
"On peut vérifier que cette matrice est hermitienne de la façon suivante :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi^{\\dagger} = \\bigl( \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\bigl( \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\\bigl( \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert = \\Pi.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi^{\\dagger} = \\bigl( \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\bigl( \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\\bigl( \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert = \\Pi.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Here, to obtain the second equality, we have used the formula\n"
msgstr "Ici, pour obtenir la seconde égalité, on a utilisé la formule\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(A B)^{\\dagger} = B^{\\dagger} A^{\\dagger},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(A B)^{\\dagger} = B^{\\dagger} A^{\\dagger},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"which is always true, for any two matrices $A$ and $B$ for which the product"
" $AB$ makes sense.\n"
msgstr ""
"qui est toujours vraie, pour deux matrices $A$ et $B$ quelconques pour "
"lesquelles le produit $AB$ a un sens.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To see that the matrix $\\Pi$ in $(4)$ is idempotent, we can use the assumption that $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is a unit vector, so that it satisfies $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi\\rangle = 1.$\n"
"Thus, we have\n"
msgstr ""
"Pour voir que la matrice $\\Pi$ dans $(4)$ est idempotente, on peut utiliser l'hypothèse que $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ est un vecteur unitaire, donc qu'il satisfait $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi\\rangle = 1.$\n"
"On a ainsi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi^2\n"
"= \\bigl( \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle \\psi\\vert \\bigr)^2\n"
"= \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle \\psi\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"= \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert = \\Pi.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi^2\n"
"= \\bigl( \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle \\psi\\vert \\bigr)^2\n"
"= \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle \\psi\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"= \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert = \\Pi.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"More generally, if $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert "
"\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ is any orthonormal set of vectors, then the matrix\n"
msgstr ""
"Plus généralement, si $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert "
"\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ est un ensemble orthonormal quelconque de vecteurs, "
"alors la matrice\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi = \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"\\tag{5}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi = \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"\\tag{5}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"is a projection.\n"
"Specifically, we have\n"
msgstr ""
"est une projection.\n"
"Plus précisément, on a\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Pi^{\\dagger}\n"
"&= \\biggl(\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\biggr)^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"&= \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\bigl(\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle\\langle\\psi_k\\vert\\bigr)^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"&= \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\\\\n"
"&= \\Pi,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Pi^{\\dagger}\n"
"&= \\biggl(\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\biggr)^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"&= \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\bigl(\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle\\langle\\psi_k\\vert\\bigr)^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"&= \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\\\\n"
"&= \\Pi,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "and\n"
msgstr "et\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Pi^2\n"
"& = \\biggl( \\sum_{j = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_j\\rangle \\langle \\psi_j \\vert\\Bigr)\\Bigl(\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\biggr) \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{j = 1}^m\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_j\\rangle \\langle \\psi_j \\vert  \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\Pi,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Pi^2\n"
"& = \\biggl( \\sum_{j = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_j\\rangle \\langle \\psi_j \\vert\\Bigr)\\Bigl(\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\biggr) \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{j = 1}^m\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_j\\rangle \\langle \\psi_j \\vert  \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\Pi,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where the orthonormality of $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert "
"\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ implies the second-to-last equality.\n"
msgstr ""
"où l'orthonormalité de $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert "
"\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ implique l'avant-dernière égalité.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In fact, this exhausts all of the possibilities: *every* projection $\\Pi$ can be written in the form $(5)$ for some choice of an orthonormal set $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert \\psi_m\\rangle\\}.$\n"
"(Technically speaking, the zero matrix $\\Pi=0,$ which is a projection, is a special case.\n"
"To fit it into the general form $(5)$ we must allow the possibility that the sum is empty, resulting in the zero matrix.)\n"
msgstr ""
"En fait, cela épuise toutes les possibilités : *toute* projection $\\Pi$ peut s'écrire sous la forme $(5)$ pour un certain choix d'ensemble orthonormal $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert \\psi_m\\rangle\\}.$\n"
"(Techniquement, la matrice nulle $\\Pi=0,$ qui est une projection, est un cas particulier.\n"
"Pour la faire entrer dans la forme générale $(5)$, on doit autoriser la possibilité que la somme soit vide, ce qui donne la matrice nulle.)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Projective measurements {#projective-measurements}"
msgstr "Mesures projectives {#projective-measurements}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The notion of a measurement of a quantum system is more general than just standard basis measurements.\n"
"*Projective measurements* are measurements that are described by a collection of projections whose sum is equal to the identity matrix.\n"
"In symbols, a collection $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ of projection matrices describes a projective measurement if\n"
msgstr ""
"La notion de mesure d'un système quantique est plus générale que les simples mesures dans la base standard.\n"
"Les *mesures projectives* sont des mesures décrites par une collection de projections dont la somme est égale à la matrice identité.\n"
"En termes symboliques, une collection $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ de matrices de projection décrit une mesure projective si\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 + \\cdots + \\Pi_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 + \\cdots + \\Pi_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When such a measurement is performed on a system $\\mathsf{X}$ while it is "
"in some state $\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ two things happen:\n"
msgstr ""
"Lorsqu'une telle mesure est effectuée sur un système $\\mathsf{X}$ alors "
"qu'il est dans un état $\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ deux choses se produisent :\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For each $k\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\},$ the outcome of the measurement is $k$ "
"with probability equal to\n"
msgstr ""
"Pour chaque $k\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\},$ le résultat de la mesure est $k$ "
"avec une probabilité égale à\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl(\\text{outcome is $k$}\\bigr) = \\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl(\\text{le résultat est $k$}\\bigr) = \\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For whichever outcome $k$ the measurement produces, the state of "
"$\\mathsf{X}$ becomes\n"
msgstr ""
"Quel que soit le résultat $k$ produit par la mesure, l'état de $\\mathsf{X}$"
" devient\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{\\Pi_k \\vert\\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\|\\Pi_k \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\bigr\\|}.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{\\Pi_k \\vert\\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\|\\Pi_k \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\bigr\\|}.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can also choose outcomes other than $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ for projective measurements if we wish.\n"
"More generally, for any finite and nonempty set $\\Sigma,$ if we have a collection of projection matrices\n"
msgstr ""
"On peut aussi choisir des résultats autres que $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ pour les mesures projectives si on le souhaite.\n"
"Plus généralement, pour tout ensemble fini et non vide $\\Sigma,$ si on dispose d'une collection de matrices de projection\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\{\\Pi_a:a\\in\\Sigma\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\{\\Pi_a:a\\in\\Sigma\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "that satisfies the condition\n"
msgstr "qui satisfait la condition\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\Pi_a = \\mathbb{I},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\Pi_a = \\mathbb{I},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"then this collection describes a projective measurement whose possible "
"outcomes coincide with the set $\\Sigma,$ where the rules are the same as "
"before:\n"
msgstr ""
"alors cette collection décrit une mesure projective dont les résultats "
"possibles coïncident avec l'ensemble $\\Sigma,$ les règles étant les mêmes "
"qu'avant :\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For each $a\\in\\Sigma,$ the outcome of the measurement is $a$ with "
"probability equal to\n"
msgstr ""
"Pour chaque $a\\in\\Sigma,$ le résultat de la mesure est $a$ avec une "
"probabilité égale à\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl(\\text{outcome is $a$}\\bigr) = \\bigl\\| \\Pi_a \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl(\\text{le résultat est $a$}\\bigr) = \\bigl\\| \\Pi_a \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For whichever outcome $a$ the measurement produces, the state of "
"$\\mathsf{X}$ becomes\n"
msgstr ""
"Quel que soit le résultat $a$ produit par la mesure, l'état de $\\mathsf{X}$"
" devient\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{\\Pi_a \\vert\\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\|\\Pi_a \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\bigr\\|}.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{\\Pi_a \\vert\\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\|\\Pi_a \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\bigr\\|}.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, standard basis measurements are equivalent to projective measurements, where $\\Sigma$ is the set of classical states of whatever system $\\mathsf{X}$ we're talking about and our set of projection matrices is\n"
"$\\{\\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert:a\\in\\Sigma\\}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Par exemple, les mesures dans la base standard sont équivalentes à des mesures projectives, où $\\Sigma$ est l'ensemble des états classiques du système $\\mathsf{X}$ dont on parle et notre ensemble de matrices de projection est\n"
"$\\{\\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert:a\\in\\Sigma\\}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Another example of a projective measurement, this time on two qubits $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y}),$ is given by the set\n"
"$\\{\\Pi_0,\\Pi_1\\},$ where\n"
msgstr ""
"Un autre exemple de mesure projective, cette fois sur deux qubits $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y}),$ est donné par l'ensemble\n"
"$\\{\\Pi_0,\\Pi_1\\},$ où\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 = \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\langle \\phi^+ \\vert + \\vert \\phi^-\\rangle\\langle \\phi^- \\vert + \\vert \\psi^+\\rangle\\langle \\psi^+ \\vert\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\Pi_1 = \\vert\\psi^-\\rangle\\langle\\psi^-\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 = \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\langle \\phi^+ \\vert + \\vert \\phi^-\\rangle\\langle \\phi^- \\vert + \\vert \\psi^+\\rangle\\langle \\psi^+ \\vert\n"
"\\quad\\text{et}\\quad\n"
"\\Pi_1 = \\vert\\psi^-\\rangle\\langle\\psi^-\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If we have multiple systems that are jointly in some quantum state and a "
"projective measurement is performed on just one of the systems, the action "
"is similar to what we had for standard basis measurements — and in fact we "
"can now describe this action in much simpler terms than we could before.\n"
msgstr ""
"Si on a plusieurs systèmes qui sont conjointement dans un état quantique et "
"qu'une mesure projective est effectuée sur un seul de ces systèmes, l'action"
" est similaire à ce qu'on avait pour les mesures dans la base standard — et "
"en fait, on peut maintenant décrire cette action en termes bien plus simples"
" qu'auparavant.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To be precise, let us suppose that we have two systems $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ in a quantum state $\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ and a projective measurement described by a collection $\\{\\Pi_a : a\\in\\Sigma\\}$ is performed on the system $\\mathsf{X},$ while nothing is done to $\\mathsf{Y}.$\n"
"Doing this is then equivalent to performing the projective measurement described by the collection\n"
msgstr ""
"Pour être précis, supposons qu'on ait deux systèmes $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ dans un état quantique $\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ et qu'une mesure projective décrite par une collection $\\{\\Pi_a : a\\in\\Sigma\\}$ soit effectuée sur le système $\\mathsf{X},$ tandis que rien n'est fait sur $\\mathsf{Y}.$\n"
"Cela est alors équivalent à effectuer la mesure projective décrite par la collection\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\{ \\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\,:\\, a\\in\\Sigma\\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\{ \\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\,:\\, a\\in\\Sigma\\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"on the joint system $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y}).$\n"
"Each measurement outcome $a$ results with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"sur le système joint $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y}).$\n"
"Chaque résultat de mesure $a$ se produit avec probabilité\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| (\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|^2,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| (\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|^2,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"and conditioned on the result $a$ appearing, the state of the joint system "
"$(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ becomes\n"
msgstr ""
"et conditionnellement au résultat $a$, l'état du système joint "
"$(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ devient\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{(\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\| (\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{(\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\| (\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Implementing projective measurements {#implementing-projective-measurements}"
msgstr ""
"Implémenter des mesures projectives {#implementing-projective-measurements}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Arbitrary projective measurements can be implemented using unitary "
"operations, standard basis measurements, and an extra workspace system, as "
"will now be explained.\n"
msgstr ""
"Des mesures projectives arbitraires peuvent être implémentées à l'aide "
"d'opérations unitaires, de mesures dans la base standard, et d'un système de"
" travail supplémentaire, comme on va l'expliquer maintenant.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let us suppose that $\\mathsf{X}$ is a system and "
"$\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ is a projective measurement on "
"$\\mathsf{X}.$ We can easily generalize this discussion to projective "
"measurements having different sets of outcomes, but in the interest of "
"convenience and simplicity we will assume the set of possible outcomes for "
"our measurement is $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Supposons que $\\mathsf{X}$ est un système et que "
"$\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ est une mesure projective sur "
"$\\mathsf{X}.$ On peut facilement généraliser cette discussion à des mesures"
" projectives ayant différents ensembles de résultats, mais par souci de "
"commodité et de simplicité, on suppose que l'ensemble des résultats "
"possibles pour notre mesure est $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let us note explicitly that $m$ is not necessarily equal to the number of "
"classical states of $\\mathsf{X}$ — we'll let $n$ be the number of classical"
" states of $\\mathsf{X},$ which means that each matrix $\\Pi_k$ is an "
"$n\\times n$ projection matrix.\n"
msgstr ""
"Notons explicitement que $m$ n'est pas nécessairement égal au nombre d'états"
" classiques de $\\mathsf{X}$ — on note $n$ le nombre d'états classiques de "
"$\\mathsf{X},$ ce qui signifie que chaque matrice $\\Pi_k$ est une matrice "
"de projection $n\\times n.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because we assume that $\\{\\Pi_0\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ represents a "
"projective measurement, it is necessarily the case that\n"
msgstr ""
"Comme on suppose que $\\{\\Pi_0\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ représente une mesure "
"projective, il est nécessairement vrai que\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\Pi_k = \\mathbb{I}_n.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\Pi_k = \\mathbb{I}_n.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Our goal is to perform a process that has the same effect as performing this"
" projective measurement on $\\mathsf{X},$ but to do this using only unitary "
"operations and standard basis measurements.\n"
msgstr ""
"Notre objectif est de réaliser un processus ayant le même effet que "
"d'effectuer cette mesure projective sur $\\mathsf{X},$ mais en n'utilisant "
"que des opérations unitaires et des mesures dans la base standard.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will make use of an extra workspace system $\\mathsf{Y}$ to do this, and specifically we'll take the classical state set of $\\mathsf{Y}$ to be $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\},$ which is the same as the set of outcomes of the projective measurement.\n"
"The idea is that we will perform a standard basis measurement on $\\mathsf{Y},$ and interpret the outcome of this measurement as being equivalent to the outcome of the projective measurement on $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"We'll need to assume that $\\mathsf{Y}$ is initialized to some fixed state, which we'll choose to be $\\vert 0\\rangle.$\n"
"(Any other choice of fixed quantum state vector could be made to work, but choosing $\\vert 0\\rangle$ makes the explanation to follow much simpler.)\n"
msgstr ""
"On va faire appel à un système de travail supplémentaire $\\mathsf{Y}$ pour cela, et plus précisément on prend l'ensemble des états classiques de $\\mathsf{Y}$ comme étant $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\},$ qui est le même que l'ensemble des résultats de la mesure projective.\n"
"L'idée est d'effectuer une mesure dans la base standard sur $\\mathsf{Y},$ et d'interpréter le résultat de cette mesure comme étant équivalent au résultat de la mesure projective sur $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"On doit supposer que $\\mathsf{Y}$ est initialisé dans un état fixe, qu'on choisit d'être $\\vert 0\\rangle.$\n"
"(Tout autre choix d'état quantique fixe pourrait être utilisé, mais choisir $\\vert 0\\rangle$ simplifie considérablement l'explication qui suit.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Of course, in order for a standard basis measurement of $\\mathsf{Y}$ to tell us anything about $\\mathsf{X},$ we will need to allow $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ to interact somehow before measuring $\\mathsf{Y},$ by performing a unitary operation on the system $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X}).$\n"
"First consider this matrix:\n"
msgstr ""
"Bien sûr, pour qu'une mesure dans la base standard de $\\mathsf{Y}$ nous donne des informations sur $\\mathsf{X},$ on devra laisser $\\mathsf{X}$ et $\\mathsf{Y}$ interagir d'une façon ou d'une autre avant de mesurer $\\mathsf{Y},$ en effectuant une opération unitaire sur le système $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X}).$\n"
"Considérons d'abord cette matrice :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\Pi_k.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\Pi_k.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Expressed explicitly as a so-called *block matrix*, which is essentially a "
"matrix of matrices that we interpret as a single, larger matrix, $M$ looks "
"like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"Exprimée explicitement comme une *matrice par blocs*, qui est "
"essentiellement une matrice de matrices qu'on interprète comme une seule "
"matrice plus grande, $M$ ressemble à ceci :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\Pi_0 & 0 & \\cdots & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_1 & 0 & \\cdots & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_{m-1} & 0 & \\cdots & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\Pi_0 & 0 & \\cdots & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_1 & 0 & \\cdots & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_{m-1} & 0 & \\cdots & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, each $0$ represents an $n\\times n$ matrix filled entirely with zeros,"
" so that the entire matrix $M$ is an $nm\\times nm$ matrix.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ici, chaque $0$ représente une matrice $n\\times n$ entièrement remplie de "
"zéros, de sorte que la matrice entière $M$ est une matrice $nm\\times nm.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now, $M$ is certainly not a unitary matrix (unless $m=1,$ in which case "
"$\\Pi_0 = \\mathbb{I},$ giving $M = \\mathbb{I}$ in this trivial case) "
"because unitary matrices cannot have any columns (or rows) that are entirely"
" $0;$ unitary matrices have columns that form orthonormal bases, and the "
"all-zero vector is not a unit vector.\n"
msgstr ""
"Or, $M$ n'est certainement pas une matrice unitaire (sauf si $m=1,$ auquel "
"cas $\\Pi_0 = \\mathbb{I},$ ce qui donne $M = \\mathbb{I}$ dans ce cas "
"trivial) car les matrices unitaires ne peuvent pas avoir de colonnes (ou de "
"lignes) entièrement nulles ; les matrices unitaires ont des colonnes qui "
"forment des bases orthonormales, et le vecteur nul n'est pas un vecteur "
"unitaire.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"However, it is the case that the first $n$ columns of $M$ are orthonormal, and we get this from the assumption that $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ is a measurement.\n"
"To verify this claim, notice that for each $j\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\},$ the vector formed by column number $j$ of $M$ is as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Cependant, il est vrai que les $n$ premières colonnes de $M$ sont orthonormales, et cela découle de l'hypothèse que $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ est une mesure.\n"
"Pour vérifier cette affirmation, remarquons que pour chaque $j\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\},$ le vecteur formé par la colonne numéro $j$ de $M$ est le suivant :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi_j\\rangle = M \\vert 0, j\\rangle = \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi_j\\rangle = M \\vert 0, j\\rangle = \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that here we're numbering the columns starting from column $0.$ Taking "
"the inner product of column $i$ with column $j$ when "
"$i,j\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}$ gives\n"
msgstr ""
"Notons qu'ici on numérote les colonnes en commençant par la colonne $0.$ Le "
"produit scalaire de la colonne $i$ avec la colonne $j$ pour "
"$i,j\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}$ donne\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle \\psi_i \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"& =\n"
"\\biggl(\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert i\\rangle\\biggr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"\\biggl(\\sum_{l = 0}^{m-1} \\vert l \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_l \\vert j\\rangle\\biggr) \\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\sum_{l = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle k \\vert l \\rangle \\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\Pi_l \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\langle i \\vert \\mathbb{I} \\vert j \\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & i = j\\\\\n"
"0 & i\\neq j,\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle \\psi_i \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"& =\n"
"\\biggl(\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert i\\rangle\\biggr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"\\biggl(\\sum_{l = 0}^{m-1} \\vert l \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_l \\vert j\\rangle\\biggr) \\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\sum_{l = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle k \\vert l \\rangle \\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\Pi_l \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\langle i \\vert \\mathbb{I} \\vert j \\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & i = j\\\\\n"
"0 & i\\neq j,\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "which is what we needed to show.\n"
msgstr "ce qui est bien ce qu'on voulait montrer.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Thus, because the first $n$ columns of the matrix $M$ are orthonormal, we "
"can replace all of the remaining zero entries by some different choice of "
"complex number entries so that the entire matrix is unitary.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ainsi, comme les $n$ premières colonnes de la matrice $M$ sont "
"orthonormales, on peut remplacer toutes les entrées nulles restantes par "
"d'autres valeurs complexes de sorte que la matrice entière soit unitaire.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\Pi_0 & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_1 & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_{m-1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\Pi_0 & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_1 & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_{m-1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If we're given the matrices $\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1},$ we can compute "
"suitable matrices to fill in for the blocks marked $\\fbox{?}$ in the "
"equation — using the Gram–Schmidt process — but it does not matter "
"specifically what these matrices are for the sake of this discussion.\n"
msgstr ""
"Si on nous donne les matrices $\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1},$ on peut calculer "
"les matrices appropriées pour remplir les blocs marqués $\\fbox{?}$ dans "
"l'équation — en utilisant le procédé de Gram–Schmidt — mais peu importe ce "
"que sont précisément ces matrices pour les besoins de cette discussion.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally we can describe the measurement process: we first perform $U$ on the joint system $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ and then measure $\\mathsf{Y}$ with respect to a standard basis measurement.\n"
"For an arbitrary state $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ of $\\mathsf{X},$ we obtain the state\n"
msgstr ""
"Enfin, on peut décrire le processus de mesure : on effectue d'abord $U$ sur le système joint $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ puis on mesure $\\mathsf{Y}$ avec une mesure dans la base standard.\n"
"Pour un état arbitraire $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ de $\\mathsf{X},$ on obtient l'état\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle \\vert \\phi\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"= M \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle \\vert \\phi\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k\\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert\\phi\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle \\vert \\phi\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"= M \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle \\vert \\phi\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k\\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert\\phi\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where the first equality follows from the fact that $U$ and $M$ agree on their first $n$ columns.\n"
"When we perform a projective measurement on $\\mathsf{Y},$ we obtain each outcome $k$ with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"où la première égalité découle du fait que $U$ et $M$ coïncident sur leurs $n$ premières colonnes.\n"
"Lorsqu'on effectue une mesure projective sur $\\mathsf{Y},$ on obtient chaque résultat $k$ avec probabilité\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle \\bigr\\|^2,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle \\bigr\\|^2,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "in which case the state of $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ becomes\n"
msgstr "auquel cas l'état de $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ devient\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert k\\rangle \\otimes \\frac{\\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle \\bigr\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert k\\rangle \\otimes \\frac{\\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle \\bigr\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Thus, $\\mathsf{Y}$ stores a copy of the measurement outcome and "
"$\\mathsf{X}$ changes precisely as it would had the projective measurement "
"described by $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ been performed directly on "
"$\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ainsi, $\\mathsf{Y}$ stocke une copie du résultat de la mesure et "
"$\\mathsf{X}$ évolue exactement comme il l'aurait fait si la mesure "
"projective décrite par $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ avait été effectuée"
" directement sur $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
